# `c2c install/uninstall muse` (settings mcpServers + skill + plugin/hooks)

## Goal

One-command attach/detach for unmanaged muse sessions. Blocked on the
B352 P4 hook-transport verdict (plugin-first vs settings.json vs
no-hooks) — implement the winner; the body covers all three shapes.

## Contract

Tables (`ocaml/cli/c2c_setup.ml`): `known_clients` :2033,
`install_subcommand_clients` :2041, `init_configurable_clients` :2044
(free `c2c install muse` routing via :786–810 group),
`do_install_client` dispatch arm :2464–2481,
`client_mcp_configured` :2536+ and `client_integration_configured`
:2636–2665 arms (file-exists like grok's — do NOT copy agy's
`_ -> false` fallthrough), `--with-mcp` set :2961 (extend ONLY if
MCP ships — B357 decides posture, this bug implements the writer),
help strings :2797/:2995. B173 analogue: decide whether muse skips
the global `~/.config/c2c/default-alias` write like grok (do so if
multi-session CLI-first).

`setup_muse` writes (mirror closest shape per P4):

- MCP (if `--with-mcp`): merge `mcpServers.c2c` stdio entry into
  `${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/muse/settings.json`.
  LOAD-BEARING: never create a legacy `mcp_servers` key alongside
  `mcpServers` (loader drops the whole member); `mode:"optional"` so
  a dead server can't block startup; literal env only (no `${VAR}`);
  env block mirrors other clients (`C2C_MCP_BROKER_ROOT`,
  `AUTO_REGISTER_ALIAS`, `AUTO_DRAIN_CHANNEL=0`, `AUTO_JOIN_ROOMS`)
  but NO static `C2C_MCP_SESSION_ID` (kimi anti-hijack precedent,
  `c2c_setup.ml:963–978`); warn that entries take effect on next
  launch only.
- Skill: owned `SKILL.md` in the muse skills dir (P4 verdict:
  personal store via `muse skills install` vs owned file write —
  prefer owned-file if the store permits c2c-managed content,
  else shell to the CLI and record the receipt accordingly).
- Hooks: plugin bundle via `muse plugins install` + `approve` (if
  non-interactive per P4 — else operator-step with exact commands),
  or `settings.json` merge (parse-tolerant, foreign keys preserved,
  agy-#65 discipline: pin the schema in a regression test, know the
  per-file vs per-hook failure scope), or nothing (skill+Monitor).
- Receive footer: Monitor arming line (grok precedent) or agentapi
  line (agy precedent) per delivery tier.

Uninstall (`ocaml/cli/c2c_uninstall.ml`): `known_components` :11,
`recompute_muse_artifacts` covering EVERY setup path (incl. any
hook-written session skill — its only remover by design, #82),
dispatch :530–540, `all` list :700. Shared files stripped
surgically (keys/blocks), never deleted; mode-preserving atomic
writes (#84 — `?perm` only for c2c-owned files).

## Acceptance

- `c2c install muse` (clean + idempotent re-run), `--dry-run`,
  `--with-mcp` / without, `--force` overwrite, manifest receipt per
  `(component,target_dir)`; `c2c uninstall muse` removes everything
  with AND without the manifest (recompute fallback); `uninstall all`
  covers muse.
- Corrupt/foreign `settings.json` (or hooks file) is never clobbered:
  merge preserves unknown keys; invalid JSON fails closed with a
  clear error, never a half-write.
- Tests `test_c2c_setup_muse.ml`: byte-equal artifacts, owned vs
  shared kinds, no-MCP-by-default (B254), merge-preserves-foreign,
  schema-shape pinned (agy-#65 style), uninstall round-trip incl.
  recompute-without-manifest, drift-only skill refresh (#82).
- Dune stanzas + `(deps c2c.exe)` where the binary is shelled to.

SCOPE (B352 verdicts, merged): plugin-first install via non-interactive plugins install <bundle> + approve <id> (per-capability trust, survives update). Gate check FIRST: if plugins list says not available in this build, fall back to settings.json hooks map (fully specified in verdict doc). Manifest covers plugin cache identity/bundle path + fallback hooks/skill keys. Uninstall verbs: remove/disable. MCP: never mcp_servers alongside mcpServers; mode optional; literal env; MUSE_SESSION_ID never static.

B173 analogue DECISION (muse skips global default-alias write, like grok): muse is multi-session CLI-first — every muse TUI/session on the host shares one machine-global ~/.config/c2c/default-alias, so letting install overwrite it would clobber other clients' bare-monitor fallback and could steer hook registrations at foreign aliases (the grok failure mode). Implemented in do_install_client (skip list [grok; muse]); verified live (no ~/.config/c2c/ created by install). Other B354 decisions: ONE skill (no c2c-session second skill — hook stdout IS the additionalContext inject, unlike grok/kimi); owned-file skill at $CONFIG_DIR/skills/c2c (direct writes honored live, no CLI receipt); fallback events SessionStart+Stop+SessionEnd; MCP entry mirrors kimi (no disabled key — --with-mcp IS explicit activation; blanket toolset per U6 CONDITIONAL).

Review-fix decisions (PIRFL, 2 native-subagent reviewers, all accepted issues fixed): (1) install-all --with-mcp set NOT extended — ticket reserves posture to B357; writer + client_mcp_configured arm ship, B357 flips the one-line gate. (2) m11 TOCTOU + m14 mid-loop exit + m16 no-lock: documented acceptances (same-uid local race, no privilege boundary; precedent-consistent exits; ms window shared by all clients). (3) LOAD-BEARING discovery: any settings.json write AFTER plugins approve resets trust to review_needed (bisected live) — install order is now install -> settings -> approve LAST; evidence in .collab/findings/2026-10-02T20-08-19Z-b354-muse-install-live-evidence.md. (4) Landing/health/wake B353 copy refreshed (landing had a duplicate muse row + false no-install claim once known_clients gained muse). Suite now 18 tests (timeout/flip/approve-fail/remove-absent/non-object-root regressions).